activities.teacherDoes:
Guide students through translating their multi-component circuit logic into a structured Arduino sketch. Model how to declare global constants for pins and structure the `setup()` and `loop()` functions. Monitor student coding workspaces, specifically checking for correct semicolon termination and block scoping in conditional statements.

Modelled Example:
const int buttonPin = 2;
const int buzzerPin = 8;
void setup() {
  pinMode(buttonPin, INPUT);
  pinMode(buzzerPin, OUTPUT);
}
void loop() {
  if (digitalRead(buttonPin) == HIGH) {
    digitalWrite(buzzerPin, HIGH);
  } else {
    digitalWrite(buzzerPin, LOW);
  }
}

